\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cost functions at $p=1$ and the hardware--simulator comparison. (a),(b) Cost functions at $p=1$ versus $s$ for (a) $\delta =-2$ and (b) $\delta =0.85$: $E_0$ (exact, blue solid) with the three initial-state costs (triv green dashed, topo orange dotted, AFM black dashdot); background bands mark the physical phases and circles mark the initial-state branch with the lowest optimized energy in each region. (c),(d) Combined quantity $Q$ for (c) $\delta =-2$ and (d) $\delta =0.85$: simulator $p=1$ (black) and $p=2$ (gray) fixed-scale curves with hardware window scatter ($p=1$, $N=500$; colors indicate the lowest-energy initial-state branches in (a),(b)). }}{6}{}}
